        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Dan Sheehan fails head injury assessment as Robert Baloucoune also goes off",
          "body": "Ireland's injury list from the Argentina win is a lengthy one. Captain Dan Sheehan, deputising for the injured Caelan Doris, was forced off in the first half after failing a head injury assessment, though Farrell said he \"seems fine in the dressing room\". Robert Baloucoune also went off with a knock in the 58th minute, Sean Jansen took a \"bang\" to his knee, and Josh van der Flier and Mack Hansen both have ankle concerns. The knocks are particularly concerning after the performance of Farrell's back three."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Quesada to name Italy's Argentina team in Thursday press release",
          "body": "Italy's team for the Argentina test in Genoa will be announced in a press release on Thursday, with Gonzalo Quesada also holding a Zoom press conference that day, the federation has confirmed. The Azzurri then hold a captain's run at the Stadio Ferraris on Friday, open to media for its first 15 minutes, before Saturday's second test of the November window. The schedule then runs on to Fiji in Udine on 21 November before the final weekend at Twickenham."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
