      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Hat-trick hero",
          "heading": "Ewan Ashman scores hat-trick in Scotland's 21-43 defeat by All Blacks",
          "body": "Ewan Ashman's three first-half tries, on 8, 27 and 38 minutes, left Scotland trailing 21-24 at the break against the All Blacks. Scotland then failed to score after the interval, and New Zealand added 19 unanswered points on their way to a 43-21 win at Murrayfield. It was Scotland's 10th defeat in their last 11 meetings with New Zealand, and the wait for a first win over them goes on."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
        }
      ]
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's verdict",
          "heading": "Dewi Lake says Wales let themselves down in Japan win",
          "body": "Captain Dewi Lake was frustrated despite the bonus-point win. \"There were massive parts of that game where we let ourselves down,\" he said, adding that the group had promised in camp to do things it probably did not manage against Japan. Josh Adams scored twice, with Archie Griffin and Louis Rees-Zammit also crossing, as Wales took the bonus point in their 28-21 win in Cardiff. Lake said the victory still mattered: \"A win is massive for this group.\" Wales now face New Zealand on Saturday."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
        }
      ],
