      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Pumas prospect Marcos Camerlinckx signs for Bath, leaving Argentina at 22",
          "body": "Bath have announced the signing of uncapped prop Marcos Camerlinckx, his first professional experience outside South America. The 22-year-old joins a front row that includes Will Stuart, Archie Griffin and Kieran Verden, and he has not yet played for Los Pumas. He recently played for the Argentina XV against the USA in Fort Lauderdale and was a Super Rugby Americas champion with Los Pampas. His father, Pablo Camerlinckx, was a No. 8 for Los Pumas, earning his final cap against Wales in 1999."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
