    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "England defeat",
          "heading": "Wallabies fall 45-22 at Twickenham despite Max Jorgensen's halftime intercept try",
          "body": "Max Jorgensen's intercept try, scored as the clock went red, pulled the Wallabies back to 19-10 behind at halftime. Henry Pollock, a makeshift winger, scored a double after being introduced on the wing, and England's four second-half tries sealed the 45-22 win. Captain Harry Wilson was blunt at full time about the Wallabies' slow start. The bench made significant inroads in the second half, with Filipo Daugunu, Rob Valetini, Taniela Tupou and Ben Donaldson of note."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship",
          "body": "South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
