      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "edition": "Monday 9 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match report",
          "heading": "Kenta Fukuda's late try falls short as Japan lose 28-21 in Cardiff",
          "body": "Japan trailed only 21-14 at half-time after Ben Gunter and captain Warner Dearns crossed, with Naoto Saito converting both. Josh Adams scored twice for Wales, and Louis Rees-Zammit also crossed before the break. Replacement scrum-half Kenta Fukuda's late try, from a passing move involving several team-mates, and Shinya Komura's conversion cut the margin to seven before Wales held on."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat Australia 45-22, Henry Pollock scoring twice",
          "body": "Fiji fall 54-17 to France in Nations Championship. South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit quits Japan to return home. France recall Marchand, Fickou and Thomas for Springboks test."
